Task 2 fix round 1 — corrected zoom evidence

Capability check with agent-browser on the local Chrome session:
  agent-browser --session task2-zoom-16b416e3e795 set viewport 1920 1080 1
  agent-browser --session task2-zoom-16b416e3e795 set media dark
  agent-browser --session task2-zoom-16b416e3e795 focus .totem-carousel-viewport
  agent-browser --session task2-zoom-16b416e3e795 press Control+plus  (five times)

Output:
{"label":"after-five-Ctrl-plus","innerWidth":1920,"innerHeight":1080,"devicePixelRatio":1,"visualViewportScale":1,"mediaMax560":false,"reducedMotion":false}

The CLI exposes DevTools viewport emulation, but no Chrome UI zoom command. CDP-dispatched Ctrl+plus remained in-page input and did not change the effective CSS viewport, so it is not browser-zoom evidence.

Corrected DevTools effective-viewport equivalent:
  agent-browser --session task2-zoom-16b416e3e795 set viewport 960 540 2
  agent-browser --session task2-zoom-16b416e3e795 focus .totem-carousel-viewport
  agent-browser --session task2-zoom-16b416e3e795 press Home

This emulates the CSS viewport (960x540) and device pixel ratio (2) that a 1920x1080, DPR 1 desktop window presents to page CSS at 200% Chrome browser zoom. It is not a literal Chrome UI zoom operation. `visualViewport.scale` remains 1 because desktop browser zoom is not pinch zoom. Normal motion remained enabled.

